{"reference":"2 Kings 22","book":"2 Kings","chapter":22,"status":"pending","sections":[{"kind":"historical_context","title":"Josiah’s response to the scroll","blocks":[{"id":"block_1","text":"The discovery of the book sets in motion the response that shapes the wider account: Josiah seeks Huldah’s word, renews the covenant, removes prohibited worship, and observes Passover. Yet the chapter also makes clear that the announced judgment on the place and its inhabitants will still come. Josiah’s humility is recognized, but it does not erase the judgment already declared.","verse_refs":["2 Kings 22:1-20"],"provenance_refs":["reader_path_2_kings_022_b2be939429d45aca1cb7a561"],"confidence":"high","interpretation_level":"fact"}]}],"generated_metadata":null}